==Description==

La commande [[Image:Silk_CubicCurve_6.svg|24px]] '''Silk CubicCurve_6''' permet de créer une courbe NURBS cubique, un objet CubicCurve_6, à partir d'un [[Image:Silk_ControlPoly6.svg|16px]] [[Silk_ControlPoly6/fr|polygone de contrôle à 6 points]].

[[File:11.-CubicCurve_6.png|300px]]

{{Caption|Un CubicCurve_6 affichant un aperçu d'une courbe cubique.}}

Il est principalement destiné à fusionner des courbes de Bézier existantes ou des [[Silk_Workbench#Curve_Segments|segments de courbe]].

[[Image:Silk_Workflow-74.png|100px]] [[Image:Button_right.svg|12px|link=]] 
[[Image:Silk_Workflow-72.png|100px]] [[Image:Button_right.svg|12px|link=]] 
[[Image:Silk_Workflow-73.png|150px]]

{{Caption|2 segments de courbe adjacents sélectionnés  → Polygone de transition → Courbe de transition obtenue}}

<span id="Usage"></span>
==Utilisation==

<div class="mw-translate-fuzzy">
# Sélectionnez un [[Image:Silk_ControlPoly6.svg|16px]] [[Silk_ControlPoly6/fr|ControlPoly6]]
# Il existe plusieurs façons de lancer la commande.
#* Cliquez sur le bouton {{Button|[[Image:Silk_CubicCurve_6.svg|16px]] CubicCurve_6}}.
#* Sélectionnez l'option {{MenuCommand|Silk → [[Image:Silk_CubicCurve_6.svg|16px]] CubicCurve_6}} du menu.
# Un objet '''CubicCurve_6''' est créé.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
==Notes==
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* A 6-control-point cubic NURBS curve. G2 continuous throughout; G3 continuous throughout except at two points along the curve, where it is G2 only.
* The practical use of this curve is to preview blends on curves before doing the full work of blending surfaces.
* This is currently an endpoint in the Silk design workflow.
* The input ControlPoly6 can be used to build grids and surfaces; alternatively, this curve can be used with the rest of FreeCAD — extruded, revolved, etc. — if curve design is all that is needed from Silk.
</div>

